0..76 Comment "// A specification monad as a theory: a monad whose computations are ordered"
77..151 Comment "// and whose extension is monotone in both its arguments (Maillard et al.,"
152..231 Comment "// \"Dijkstra Monads for All\", ICFP 2019, § 3.3). An operation lands in a sort,"
232..305 Comment "// not in `Type`, so the order is a sort indexed by two computations, and"
306..383 Comment "// evidence of it is a term its operations build. The monad\'s laws beside the"
384..432 Comment "// indexed sort are refused in the twin (#1510)."
434..506 Comment "/// Values `V`, computations `C` and the order between two computations:"
507..574 Comment "/// reflexive, transitive, and an extension below another where its"
575..625 Comment "/// computation and each of its continuations are."
626..628 Other "@["
629..635 Other "checks"
636..637 Other "]"
